{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/pulls/1174","id":4958124596,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUoK9js8AAAABJ4b6NA","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/pull/1174","diff_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/pull/1174.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/pull/1174.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/issues/1174","number":1174,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"T-2979, T-2980, T-2981: Refine parked period wagons and carriage","user":{"login":"kevinrhaas","id":4193586,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTM1ODY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4193586?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Park three refined 1835 farm wagons and two curved-canvas covered wagons at their existing yard stands, plus an empty 1904 carriage on Prairie Avenue. Each covered wagon keeps its original blue/oxide or oak/dark-oak finish, aging seed, location, bearing and laid-by yoke. Light, distance and load-failure fallbacks remain available. Maker and ownership are unknown; the 1904 carriage is a reconstructed generic type.\n\n![Western Hotel covered wagon](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kevinrhaas/chicago-tickets/main/evidence/parked-vehicles-2026-10-22/checkpoint-combined-vehicle-preflight/source-desktop-western-front-quarter-refined.png)\n\n![Wolf Point covered wagon](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kevinrhaas/chicago-tickets/main/evidence/parked-vehicles-2026-10-22/checkpoint-combined-vehicle-preflight/source-desktop-wolfpoint-front-quarter-refined.png)\n\nFull detail with active Ghost views receives a measured allowance of 8,900 driver draws and 3,675,000 triangles. At the same controlled pose, parent/current Normal, X-ray and Ghost-40 counts were 3,694/8,222/8,465 versus 3,695/8,223/8,466. Only one shadow-yard draw differs; both versions exceeded the ordinary-view calibration. Actual GL agrees with the shipped counter, with zero private picking draws. The allowance uses the retained CI peak of 8,469 plus 5%, rounded to 100, and the parent X-ray peak of 3,656,436 triangles plus the existing 18,059 margin, rounded to 5,000. Ordinary views, Balanced, Light and higher inspection allowances retain their limits. Public and frame-stat budgets agree and restore when Ghost ends.\n\nThe Python 3.11 CI gate exposed a source-reproduction failure hidden by local Python 3.12. Ten floating sums in three authoring files now use explicit math.fsum. Native 3.11 and root 3.12 independently reproduce the original raw-parts digest and all three shipped wagon GLBs exactly, with every original input/output guard and recipe intact. Three sidecars differ only in source-code provenance hashes; runtime JavaScript, model bytes, textures, scene data and budgets are unchanged by this repair.\n\nValidation: full local preflight under CI-matching CPython 3.11.17 passed all 1,041 checks, including 380 deliberate refusal self-tests. Exact PR-diff and own-commit changelog/ID checks passed. Native 3.11 reproduced the old failure and then all original model hashes; root 3.12 independently repeated the production wrappers. Independent source/provenance review passed. Post-commit publish and mirror validation passed at `dd147cae0e85f9e39855d0d130da19e782f7eecb`. Earlier actual main-scene evidence includes 22 normal covered-wagon images, 82 frames and 14 selected root image reviews. Fresh normal CI at this new repair commit is pending.\n\nRuntime coverage: the original 18 published smoke jobs were dispatched once at `e694849a2c516a9862a2564c5ff86d97406e09ab`. Seventeen are now strictly bound to successful actual jobs/logs, including every mobile cell; desktop part 13 remains running. These remain e694 jobs. The source/asset equivalence proof binds the repair tree `5badfa088cfeb4ff9c86e31a1d2221a09c790db3`: every renderer file is unchanged except the source_sha256 field in three sidecars, whose remaining JSON is identical; all scene data, recipes and reviewed GLBs are exact. This supports retaining their runtime coverage for the authoring-only repair. Fresh normal checks and ordinary current-head merge checks remain required; no DEV merge or all-green claim.\n\nThe calibration follows AGENTS.md's measured-headroom ruling. It changes the declared allowance; rendering work, geometry and transparency order are unchanged. Original failed CI and stopped diagnostics are retained. Parent/current arms ran in separate executions with exact pose, state and prebuilt bindings. The historic CI pose is unknown and local Ghost differs by three draws; this is not an all-camera or frame-rate guarantee. [Saved evidence and handover](https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago-tickets/tree/main/evidence/parked-vehicles-2026-10-22).\n\nThis consolidates the covered-wagon source from closed draft #1176. T-2979 is the initial visible placement increment; T-2980 stays open for photographic and compressed-LOD acceptance. Fine cloth, wood and iron finishing, occupied collision, people, horses, motion and boarding remain open. The generic carriage is not identified as Studebaker, Pullman or Dearborn. DEV integration only after relevant green checks; no production promotion.\n","created_at":"2026-10-21T20:46:17Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T02:12:07Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"74a5e7eec3cbe722a07e10cadff487cadbf343b4","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/pulls/1174/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/pulls/1174/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/issues/1174/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/statuses/dd147cae0e85f9e39855d0d130da19e782f7eecb","head":{"label":"kevinrhaas:steward/parked-period-vehicles-20261021","ref":"steward/parked-period-vehicles-20261021","sha":"dd147cae0e85f9e39855d0d130da19e782f7eecb","user":{"login":"kevinrhaas","id":4193586,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTM1ODY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4193586?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":{"id":1384299918,"node_id":"R_kgDOUoK9jg","name":"chicago","full_name":"kevinrhaas/chicago","private":false,"owner":{"login":"kevinrhaas","id":4193586,"